the target language is: lps.

% The third LE1 specimen, re-expressed in LE2 idiom.
% Source: legacy_lps1/examples/CLOUT_workshop/RockPaperScissorsEthereumFEn.pl
% Covers: prolog events, a composite event (l_events), an intensional fluent
% (l_int) with an aggregate.
%
% The Ethereum bridge itself -- e_transaction, e_getBalance, e_sendTransaction,
% lps_my_account -- is external Prolog, so it lives in the companion file
% rock_paper_scissors_ethereum.lps (docs/le_lps_surface.md §7).

the maximum time is 120.

the prolog events are:
    *an address* sends *an input* worth *an amount* to *a second address*; known as e_transaction.

the actions are:
    *a player* pays *a prize*; known as pay.

the fluents are:
    the game is over; known as gameOver.
    *a player* has played *a choice*; known as played.
    the reward is *a number*; known as reward.
    the players are *a number*; known as num_players.

the templates are:
    *a choice* beats *another choice*.
    *an address* is my account; known as lps_my_account.
    the balance of *an address* is *a value*; known as e_getBalance.
    *an address* sends *a prize* to *a player* as *a payment*; known as e_sendTransaction.
    *a payment* has a receipt; known as e_existsTransactionReceipt.

the knowledge base rock paper scissors ethereum includes:

scissors beats paper.
paper beats rock.
rock beats scissors.

when an address sends an input worth an amount to a second address
    and the second address is my account
    and the amount > 0
    and it is not the case that the address has played a second choice
then the address has played the input.

the reward is a number at a time if
    an address is my account
    and the balance of the address is a value
    and the number is 0.9 * the value.

the players are a number at a time if
    the number is the count of each a player
        such that the player has played a value at the time.

it must not be true that
    the players are a number at a time
    and the number > 2.

a player pays a prize from a first time to a second time if
    an address is my account
    and the address sends the prize to the player as a payment
    and the payment has a receipt at the second time.

if a first player has played a first choice at a first time
    and a second player has played a second choice at the first time
    and the first player is different from the second player
    and the first choice beats the second choice
    and it is not the case that the game is over at the first time
then initiate the game is over from the first time to a second time
    and the reward is a prize at the first time
    and the first player pays the prize from the first time to a second time.

if a first player has played a first choice at a first time
    and a second player has played the first choice at the first time
    and the first player is different from the second player
    and it is not the case that the game is over at the first time
then initiate the game is over from the first time to a second time
    and the reward is a prize at the first time
    and a number is the prize / 2
    and the first player pays the number from the first time to a second time
    and the second player pays the number from the first time to the second time.
